From cb7c21b135048d4214cc7b1a482e2d9073e8e752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:27:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Desktop sidebar folds to an icon rail

Eugene asked for a desktop sidebar that can be squeezed to icons and
expanded again. At lg and up, the sidebar's header now has Collapse; the
rail (88px) keeps every destination as an icon with a short label (Create,
Discover, Progress, Me in v4+; the v1-v3 set otherwise), New session as
a round button on top, notifications, invite and help as icons, and
Expand at the foot. Recent sessions and the build badge stay in the full
sidebar. The choice is remembered per browser (aurelia.sidebar.rail).

Fixed bars beside the sidebar (Story, Session details, Session settings)
now read its width from --app-sidebar instead of a hard 260px, so they
follow the rail. Below lg nothing changes: the drawer has no collapse.
Staging only (RELEASES.sidebarRail).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
